# One line. Run from the repo root by `orgasmic verify TASK-RMA18.1`.
#
# `env -u ...` because a dispatch leaks its run id and home into subprocesses,
# and this test boots its own daemon against a temp home that must see neither.
#
# ONE test, and it is the whole finding: a managed worktree containing an
# INITIALIZED SUBMODULE that holds an untracked sentinel. `git worktree remove`
# refuses such a worktree outright, before it considers cleanliness, and
# TASK-RMA18 reproduced only git's locked and unclean refusals — so
# `worktree-prune` recursively deleted a tree git itself declines to touch
# without `--force`.
#
# The fixture commits `submodule.vendor/sub.ignore = all` into `.gitmodules`,
# which is what makes this DATA LOSS rather than a parity wart: the parent then
# reports the tree CLEAN, so no salvage runs at all. Salvage could not have
# helped anyway — `git add -A` records a submodule as a gitlink, so nothing
# inside one ever reaches a salvage commit.
#
# The other half of the finding, `--ignore-submodules=none` on the clean check,
# is reverted by the same injection and is not separately observable here: the
# submodule refusal fires first, exactly as it does in git. It is pinned by the
# fixture's own premise assertions instead, which fail loudly if `git status`
# ever stops reporting this tree clean.
env -u ORGASMIC_RUN_ID -u ORGASMIC_HOME cargo test -p orgasmic-cli --test dispatch worktree_prune_refuses_a_worktree_containing_an_initialized_submodule
